            <div xml:id="d840">

                <pb facs="0688" n="572" xml:id="pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12612.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to Mexico to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. As stated in my No. 96, July 24, the President appointed today as his
                    delegates to the conference with the Constitutionalists the following: General
                    Lauro Villar, Chief Justice of the Supreme Military Court, and Licenciado David
                    Gutiérrez Allende, Associate Justice of the Supreme Court of Mexico, who will
                    leave tomorrow morning accompanied by one secretary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
